# Git and pull request routing

Only `git-good` may mutate Git or pull requests. Other agents may use only `git status`, `git log`, `git diff`, and `git show`.

Route mutations through `.cursor/agents/git-good.md` and the canonical skill at `/agent/repos/docfoundry-skills/.cursor/skills/git-good/SKILL.md`.

Require a Jira `KAN-*` key. Prefer `cursor/KAN-<n>-<descriptive-name>-<run-id>` branches. Feature work branches from `dev`, then merges into `dev` and pushes `dev` after checks — no pull request into `dev`. Pull requests are required only into `main`. Sync merged hotfixes back to `dev` by merge/push without a sync pull request. Hand status updates to `work-manager`. Do not let `git-good` mutate Jira or Confluence.

Never merge a GitHub pull request without an explicit user instruction.

Bootstrap exception: the parent may create the installation commit for `git-good` only when `git-good` does not yet exist.
